lsen","locid":"173d2ddd-08a1-4ce7-bf73-0dc942ea1c19","name":"Michaelsen, Signe Regner","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Bjarne Winther","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"c86dd558-a0f0-4045-9b6f-2f41afe884fc","name":"Kristensen, Bjarne Winther","orcid":"0000-0002-6352-0826","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39251578"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-024-52167-y","issn":["20411723"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"7857","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85203345816"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-7d396d89-c669-4da9-b830-9409a62523e8","ku-afb7fc9d-0274-4dc2-9dcb-69c05d15b222"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Glioblastoma cells increase expression of notch signaling and synaptic genes within infiltrated brain tissue","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-768303","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Despite significant recent advances, artificial agents are still far behind biological agents in their abilities to adapt to novel and unexpected situations. This thesis contributes to the field of adaptive artificial agents, taking inspiration from biology to develop new methods that extend the capabilities of artificial agents controlled by neural networks. Several methods are introduced: (a) An algorithm, named Evolve & Merge, that progressively decreases the number of plasticity rules used to update the synapses of a neural network until the number of rules is orders of magnitude smaller than the number of rules. This is done without diminishing the agent’s performance and without extending the overall training time; (b) A parameterization of neurons in a neural network that makes each neuron a tiny dynamical system. These neurons are shown to be expressive enough to solve several reinforcement learning (RL) tasks even when no synapses are optimized and only the parameters of the neurons are evolved in random neural networks; (c) A meta-learning framework that optimizes a network to provide a reward signal for an RL agent. The evolved reward signal is shown to enhance the training stability of the RL agent as well as enable the agent to maintain performance in novel circumstances through continued optimization with the evolved reward signal; (d) A demonstration of the minimal requirements for agents to become invariant to permutations of the input elements as well as the size of the input and output vectors; (e) A framework, named Structurally Flexible Adaptive Neural Networks (SFANN) that combines ideas from the earlier contributions of the thesis. SFANNs have a small number of plasticity rules, parameterized dynamic neurons, the ability to learn from rewards, and are flexible in the structure both when it comes to the input and output, and the hidden layers. This framework is put forward as a method that can be optimized in environments of different input and output dimensions to eventually allow a single set of parameters to serve as a general learner across many contexts.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Winther Pedersen, Joachim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718838"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bio inspired approaches to adaptive artificial agents","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/109068413/PhD_Thesis_Final_Version_Joachim_Winther_Pedersen.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718838","ids":["itu-2b01c277-1c11-4d53-a676-e3f8d9b0dcbe"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7E68D4CB38AE2058BC3E6CF394BE173D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/109068413/PhD_Thesis_Final_Version_Joachim_Winther_Pedersen.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joachim","key":"wintherpedersenpau","last":"Winther Pedersen","locid":"ff6f398b-4bde-46da-a460-9815134b42eb","name":"Winther Pedersen, Joachim","orcid":"0000-0001-7884-9432","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788779494084"],"issn":["16023536"],"issue":"212","pages":"225","place":"Copenhagen","publisher":"IT University of Copenhagen","series":"ITU-DS","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2b01c277-1c11-4d53-a676-e3f8d9b0dcbe"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Bio-Inspired Approaches to Adaptive Artificial Agents","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718838","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"ABSTRACT Organisms in nature have evolved to exhibit flexibility in face of changes to the environment and/or to themselves. Artificial neural networks (ANNs) have proven useful for controlling of artificial agents acting in environments. However, most ANN models used for reinforcement learning-type tasks have a rigid structure that does not allow for varying input sizes. Further, they fail catastrophically if inputs are presented in an ordering unseen during optimization. We find that these two ANN inflexibilities can be mitigated and their solutions are simple and highly related. For permutation invariance, no optimized parameters can be tied to a specific index of the input elements. For size invariance, inputs must be projected onto a common space that does not grow with the number of projections. Based on these restrictions, we construct a conceptually simple model that exhibit flexibility most ANNs lack. We demonstrate the model’s properties on multiple control problems, and show that it can cope with even very rapid permutations of input indices, as well as changes in input size. Ablation studies show that is possible to achieve these properties with simple feedforward structures, but that it is much easier to optimize recurrent structures.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Winther Pedersen, Joachim","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381906"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Artificial neural networks","Feedforward Structures","Flexibility in Artificial Agents","Permutation Invariance","Recurrent neural networks","Reinforcement learning","Size Invariance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"minimal neural network models for permutation invariant agents","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2205.07868.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381906","ids":["itu-2b41decf-c75e-4ecf-be2e-497eb8f0fc66"],"keyword":["Artificial Neural Networks","Feedforward Structures","Flexibility in Artificial Agents","Permutation Invariance","Recurrent Neural Networks","Reinforcement Learning","Size Invariance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D5985B1F8364F1CBEF5BC19D5605AB79"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2205.07868.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joachim","key":"wintherpedersenpau","last":"Winther Pedersen","locid":"ff6f398b-4bde-46da-a460-9815134b42eb","name":"Winther Pedersen, Joachim","orcid":"0000-0001-7884-9432","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2b41decf-c75e-4ecf-be2e-497eb8f0fc66"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Minimal Neural Network Models for Permutation Invariant Agents","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381906","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
